cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Rolling Context — verified context compression for LLM sessions,
  with a Lean 4 formalization
message: >-
  If you use this software or refer to its formalization in academic work,
  please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Saimono
    alias: Saimonokuma
    affiliation: Nova-Violet Role
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/Nova-Violet-Role/claude-rolling-context-Lean-4-
url: https://github.com/Nova-Violet-Role
abstract: >-
  A transparent proxy that gives LLM coding sessions rolling context
  compression: older messages are replaced by a model-written summary while
  recent messages remain verbatim, so a session's input cost grows linearly
  rather than quadratically and the context window is never exhausted.

  The compression policy is formalized in Lean 4 — 157 machine-checked
  theorems with no `sorry`. The central result, pinned_never_cut, establishes
  that for any conversation, any policy, and any number of compression rounds,
  the pinned messages that come out are exactly the pinned messages that went
  in. Retention is structural rather than a request made of the summarizing
  model. Two companion theorems complete the guarantee: run_shrinks (the
  result is never larger than the input) and run_fixpoint (iteration strictly
  decreases and halts).

  The development is mutation-tested, which distinguishes theorems that
  constrain behaviour from those that are merely true: of 116 theorems in the
  compressor module, 102 are load-bearing under 66 injected mutations.

  Ships as a Claude Code plugin and as a port to the Mistral Vibe CLI.
keywords:
  - formal verification
  - Lean 4
  - theorem proving
  - context compression
  - large language models
  - mutation testing
  - proxy
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
